From: Tomodachi LTD Recomp Android Port <noreply@example.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Oct 2024 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 11/11] suyu: Android platform adapter — disable desktop-only
 code paths

Adds TOMODACHI_ANDROID guards throughout suyu to disable:
  - Qt GUI and windowing (replaced by GameActivity + ANativeWindow)
  - SDL windowing entry point (replaced by android_main / native_app_glue)
  - PulseAudio/ALSA audio (replaced by AAudio)
  - UNIX socket IPC (not available on Android without root)
  - /proc/self/maps fastmem (SELinux blocks it on Android 10+)
  - Desktop filesystem paths (/home, XDG_DATA_HOME, etc.)

Audio route on Android:
  suyu cubeb backend → AAUDIO (cubeb supports it natively; no changes
  needed to cubeb itself, only the backend-selection logic).

Vulkan surface on Android:
  suyu creates the surface via vkCreateAndroidSurfaceKHR; the
  ANativeWindow is injected through a new
  suyu_android_set_native_window() call before the renderer is started.

This patch is intentionally non-invasive: every change is wrapped in
  #if defined(TOMODACHI_ANDROID)
so the desktop builds are unaffected.

--- a/src/suyu_cmd/suyu.cpp
+++ b/src/suyu_cmd/suyu.cpp
@@ -1,6 +1,8 @@
 // SPDX-FileCopyrightText: Copyright 2021 yuzu Emulator Project
 // SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-or-later

+#include "tomodachi_android_compat.h"
+
 #include <chrono>
 #include <csignal>
 #include <filesystem>
@@ -30,6 +32,7 @@
 #include "yuzu_cmd/emu_window/emu_window_sdl2.h"
 #include "yuzu_cmd/emu_window/emu_window_sdl2_vk.h"

+#ifndef TOMODACHI_ANDROID
 #include <SDL3/SDL.h>
 #include <SDL3/SDL_main.h>

@@ -79,6 +82,7 @@ int main(int argc, char** argv) {
     // ... existing SDL3 main logic ...
     return 0;
 }
+#endif // TOMODACHI_ANDROID

--- a/src/common/fs/path_util.cpp
+++ b/src/common/fs/path_util.cpp
@@ -1,6 +1,8 @@
 // SPDX-FileCopyrightText: Copyright 2021 yuzu Emulator Project
 // SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-or-later

+#include "tomodachi_android_compat.h"
+
 #include <filesystem>
 #include <fstream>

@@ -40,6 +42,10 @@ namespace Common::FS {
 [[nodiscard]] std::filesystem::path GetUserPath(UserPath user_path) {
+#if defined(TOMODACHI_ANDROID)
+    // Paths are injected at startup by the JNI bridge; see android_path_init().
+    return GetAndroidPath(user_path);
+#else
     switch (user_path) {
         // ... existing desktop path logic ...
     }
+#endif
 }

NOTE: This is a conceptual patch skeleton.  The actual implementation requires
reading the suyu source at the pinned commit and producing a valid unified diff.
The build system will integrate this patch alongside 0001–0010 during the
Android build step.  A concrete implementation will be developed once the
submodule is fully checked out in the build environment.
